The marks on this triangle show which sides are equal. Classify it according to its side properties.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.95]
\tikzset{tickmark/.style={postaction={decorate,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.5 with {\draw (0pt,-4pt)--(0pt,4pt);}}}}}
\coordinate (B) at (0,0);
\coordinate (C) at (3.8,0);
\coordinate (A) at (1.9,3.4);
\draw[tickmark] (A) -- (B);
\draw[tickmark] (A) -- (C);
\draw (B) -- (C);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Classify this triangle according to its side properties.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.95]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (4,0);
\coordinate (C) at (2,3.4641);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway,below,font=\small] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway,above right,font=\small] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\draw (C) -- (A) node[midway,above left,font=\small] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Classify this triangle according to its angle properties.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.95]
\coordinate (B) at (0,0);
\coordinate (C) at (4.4,0);
\coordinate (A) at (2.1233,2.2771);
\draw (B) -- (C) -- (A) -- cycle;
\pic[draw,"$47^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.62cm,angle eccentricity=1.85] {angle=C--B--A};
\pic[draw,"$45^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.62cm,angle eccentricity=1.85] {angle=A--C--B};
\pic[draw,"$88^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.45cm,angle eccentricity=2.3] {angle=B--A--C};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Classify $\Delta PQR$ according to its angle properties.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.95]
\coordinate (P) at (0,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (4,0);
\coordinate (R) at (1.2,1.833);
\draw (P) -- (Q) -- (R) -- cycle;
\coordinate (ra) at ($(R)!0.3cm!(P)$);
\coordinate (rb) at ($(R)!0.3cm!(Q)$);
\draw (ra) -- ($(ra)+(rb)-(R)$) -- (rb);
\node[below left] at (P) {$P$};
\node[below right] at (Q) {$Q$};
\node[above] at (R) {$R$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Classify this triangle according to both its side and its angle properties.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.95]
\tikzset{tickmark/.style={postaction={decorate,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.5 with {\draw (0pt,-4pt)--(0pt,4pt);}}}}}
\coordinate (B) at (0,0);
\coordinate (C) at (5,0);
\coordinate (A) at (2.5,1.5023);
\draw[tickmark] (A) -- (B);
\draw[tickmark] (A) -- (C);
\draw (B) -- (C);
\pic[draw,"$118^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.45cm,angle eccentricity=2.5] {angle=B--A--C};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

In $\Delta RST$ below, which angle is opposite the side $RS$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.95]
\coordinate (R) at (0,0);
\coordinate (S) at (3.6,0);
\coordinate (T) at (1.1,2.5);
\draw (R) -- (S) -- (T) -- cycle;
\node[below left] at (R) {$R$};
\node[below right] at (S) {$S$};
\node[above] at (T) {$T$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Mia writes that this triangle is **obtuse-angled and scalene**.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.95]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (4.2,0);
\coordinate (C) at (2.1,1.393);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway,below,font=\small] {$10\text{ cm}$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway,above right,font=\small] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\draw (C) -- (A) node[midway,above left,font=\small] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\pic[draw,"$113^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.42cm,angle eccentricity=2.6] {angle=A--C--B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Which statement about Mia's naming is correct?
